---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
const sessions = (await getCollection('sessions')).sort((a, b) => a.data.number - b.data.number);
---
<Base title="WAGademy — a self-paced course on getting research done">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Six sessions · at your own pace</p>
      <h1>The thesis isn't writing itself.</h1>
      <p>
        WAGademy started as a six-week Working Accountability Group for HDR students at UQ:
        a themed discussion, then three hours of focused work, alongside other people doing the same.
        This is the whole thing, written up so you can work through it alone — or run it for your own group.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="/sessions/1/">Start with session 1</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" style="border-color:var(--cream);color:var(--cream)" href="/timer/">Open the timer</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How to use this</h2>
      <p>
        Each session is a short read — twenty to thirty minutes — followed by something concrete to do.
        They stand alone, so you can jump to whichever problem is currently yours. But the order isn't
        arbitrary: session 1 sets up the goal-setting method the rest assume.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/sessions/4/">Session 4</a> is different. It's a hands-on walkthrough: work through it at a
        laptop for an hour and you finish with a real project on GitHub, a sane folder structure and a README.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>The six sessions</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      {sessions.map((s) => (
        <a class="card" href={`/sessions/${s.data.number}/`}>
          <span class="num">Session {s.data.number} · {s.data.minutes} min</span>
          {s.data.kind === 'hands-on' && <span class="badge hands-on" style="margin-left:.5rem">Hands-on</span>}
          <h3>{s.data.title}</h3>
          <p>{s.data.blurb}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The method, in three steps</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Commit.</strong> Say your goals out loud, and write them somewhere visible.</li>
        <li><strong>Work.</strong> Three 50-minute pomodoros, phones away, alongside other people.</li>
        <li><strong>Report.</strong> Did you hit it? What got in the way? No judgment — it's data.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        That's it. Everything else on this site is detail. If you want to run this for your own group,
        <a href="/run-your-own/">here's how</a> — it needs a room, a timer, and three other people.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
